"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does molecular-dynamics verification of viscosity and thermal conductivity reorder a machine-learning ester shortlist, and does the best coolant keep improving?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Molecular dynamics reorders the shortlist: machine-learning viscosity error (22.467% MAPE) exceeds molecular-dynamics error, so better esters appear after verification [s3].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s3\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4/tables/2\",\"quote\":\"our work 9.233 22.467 12.528 3.978 2.911\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:sequential_part\",\"text\":\"Each candidate's viscosity waits on one long trajectory; the ranking waits on 100, 300, then 1000 candidates.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:method\",\"text\":\"Split each long trajectory into independent replicas on separate GPUs, block-average the Green-Kubo integrals, and run candidates side by side.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"By 100 candidates the replica ranking matches the sequential baseline, diverges from machine-learning, and the best figure climbs through 1000.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Replicas match the sequential ranking only by 300 candidates; then molecular dynamics confirms the machine-learning list from 100 through 1000.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Run Green-Kubo molecular dynamics on the top 100 then 300 of 461 monoesters [s1]. Compare MD-vs-ML rank correlation and figure climb. Time single-trajectory against parallel replicas.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"Based on the aforementioned criteria of the kinematic viscosity and thermal conductivity, 461 monoesters are finally filtered out.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"A 2026 benchmark ran Green-Kubo molecular dynamics on eight organic liquids; viscosity ranking stayed, thermal conductivity did not [s9][s7][s8].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s6\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"Production was carried out in the NVT ensemble for 8 ns per replica to allow the slow shear-stress autocorrelation tail to converge.\"},{\"id\":\"s9\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"we apply Green–Kubo MD simulations to eight molecules, two from each of the four principal chemical families of the dataset, at 40 °C and 100 °C.\"},{\"id\":\"s7\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"Despite these limitations, the force field largely preserves the ordering of the reference viscosity values for the eight fluids at both temperatures, suggesting that MD simulations remain useful for relative screening, even where its absolute viscosity predictions require caution.\"},{\"id\":\"s8\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"Unlike the viscosity, the LOPLS force field does not reproduce even the relative ordering of the thermal conductivities of the eight fluids.\"}],\"value\":8}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Only eight molecules had viscosity and thermal conductivity Green-Kubo verified against reference values [s9]; the 100-to-1000 shortlist answer is open.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s9\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"we apply Green–Kubo MD simulations to eight molecules, two from each of the four principal chemical families of the dataset, at 40 °C and 100 °C.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Green-Kubo molecular dynamics reproduces the paper's measured Ester 1 viscosity 6.41 cSt and conductivity 0.141 W/m K.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s4\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4/tables/4\",\"quote\":\"Ester 1 2.80 3.13 6.41 7.18 1.98 2.23 0.141 0.144\"}],\"value\":6.41}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows single-phase ranking under one force field and 15 ns sampling; no synthesis, dielectric, flammability, compatibility, or stability checks. The 1000-candidate run exceeds the budget.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s3\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4/tables/2\",\"quote\":\"our work 9.233 22.467 12.528 3.978 2.911\",\"supports\":\"ML viscosity MAPE 22.467% at 40 C\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s1\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"Based on the aforementioned criteria of the kinematic viscosity and thermal conductivity, 461 monoesters are finally filtered out.\",\"supports\":\"the 461-monoester shortlist and the ML-only screen MD is inserted into\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s9\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"we apply Green–Kubo MD simulations to eight molecules, two from each of the four principal chemical families of the dataset, at 40 °C and 100 °C.\",\"supports\":\"the prior's scope: eight molecules, four chemical families, 40 and 100 C\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s7\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"Despite these limitations, the force field largely preserves the ordering of the reference viscosity values for the eight fluids at both temperatures, suggesting that MD simulations remain useful for relative screening, even where its absolute viscosity predictions require caution.\",\"supports\":\"the prior's finding that MD largely preserves the viscosity ranking\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s8\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"Unlike the viscosity, the LOPLS force field does not reproduce even the relative ordering of the thermal conductivities of the eight fluids.\",\"supports\":\"the prior's finding that MD misorders thermal conductivity\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s4\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4/tables/4\",\"quote\":\"Ester 1 2.80 3.13 6.41 7.18 1.98 2.23 0.141 0.144\",\"supports\":\"Ester 1 measured viscosity 6.41 cSt and conductivity 0.141 W/m K\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s6\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13647254\",\"quote\":\"Production was carried out in the NVT ensemble for 8 ns per replica to allow the slow shear-stress autocorrelation tail to converge.\",\"supports\":\"the closest prior's compute quantity (8) and its 8 ns per replica production protocol\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:a100_usd_gpu_h\",\"name\":\"A100 on-demand price\",\"value\":1.99,\"unit\":\"USD/GPU-h\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU: 40 GB | vCPUs: 124 | RAM: 1800 GiB | STORAGE: 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.99 (* plus applicable sales tax/VAT/GST)\",\"url\":\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:a100_ns_day\",\"name\":\"A100 GROMACS throughput\",\"value\":267.5,\"unit\":\"ns/day\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2\",\"page_setting\":\"NHR@FAU GROMACS 2024.1 benchmark, System 1 (R-143a in hexane, 20,248 atoms)\",\"differs_in\":[\"system: R-143a in hexane, 20,248 atoms, versus a ~15,000-atom saturated monoester box\",\"the benchmark writes energy output 333x more often and loses 2.6x; our Green-Kubo runs also write pressure and heat flux at high frequency\"],\"url\":\"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus\"}

